    <briefdescription>
<para>Carries mouse event data for the mouse signals. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>An instance of this class is passed to each mouse signal. Mirrors the Qt <computeroutput>QEvent</computeroutput> API: call <computeroutput><ref refid="classQAccelPlot_1_1PlotMouseEvent_1a7944913d23a28ca9e24c274b505af679" kindref="member">accept()</ref></computeroutput> in a handler to consume the event and suppress the plot&apos;s built-in handling (dragging, double-click rescaling, etc.).</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>The object is owned by <computeroutput><ref refid="classQAccelPlot_1_1QAccelPlot" kindref="compound">QAccelPlot</ref></computeroutput> and is reused across events — do not store a reference to it beyond the signal handler. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
